   "date": "2017-03-30T13:20:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] methylkit/eDMR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">One other note is that the paper you mentioned applies far more filters to the other tools than methylKit/eDMR (Figure 2), which make the comparison between the tools a bit of apples to oranges.<div><a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/bib/article-lookup/doi/10.1093/bib/bbv095\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://academic.oup.com/bib/article-lookup/doi/10.1093/bib/bbv095&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793232627592000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33sJRij8lYFzQSidVAUuYX\">https://academic.oup.com/bib/article-lookup/doi/10.1093/bib/bbv095</a></div><div><br></div><div>Other are limited to 0.9 quantile, which would dramatically change the results, along with some of the other filters.</div><div><br><div><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/AKElOhbRcX50yR7SLpsje6Yo1vX2AoBtmTrOuD16nJxo9EzluxgaEjbrVHO_nv8Vvw-SSc_p5A6sOhbwV2aDbMN9VMuaHYfPU61P5QCoMFCiDcnRQXXe8eaMvUGMBpQUUdI9FF_ARXtfo7Jr2vN3q9ygORImoLAOCsHRGdAaCPfDDeJOgwtymUYkcgRJgn8osKzHCy7JhozFs7A5XtcqooVYsJuT4XjZcuqOqfGYVibeHnGGv0b84y1LjIeUsRP3d_DZGw-vHzUc6RdaTIfenfI6XksrG2mru699XIIoVDU-6DGJMhdIjWub6J6j_G69iSScDnroQWsZswY5wUTt7muO0Eeq9JNaLVE74vyrmiwMlJS7EVfM7Tt7-DtgKi1mFou-2587Tvcknvi0EYahlglT9twssrTNn5DWBs3-daCpynoxdsb-X_i2yyzu2-V6hgX9zBbFQqJOE7B0C9jdATas5QX97rZWIOciWPpTkhxwTOUOm-4O4lVnKYP0AzVhNiSoWkPwHpInPKjlNiZ5OYp8o_7nU1Av6Kt1twjDlILrCeae5AqpMcefI53Eca7nflO8uKGkxID9gki-ER9oWGe9Gg5wo-50D_qoS__eeXDn6x87ye8mMt29zrdZJu4jIw2D4Qk-yqanDKyjDJEaMk8rxZ1Avlgl8O_lsJbifE-op_sMWt6DOokKpjmlYV36zNmeJerR2UQNSKGlMXtdOFcD_78S0Skv-TE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://oup.silverchair-cdn.com/oup/backfile/Content_public/Journal/bib/17/5/10.1093_bib_bbv095/2/m_bbv095f2p.png?Expires=1490972949&amp;Signature=DxriMJ1BF%7E9YrSi%7E2zqmZaMKYyKlFtQH3m3yaqekyG-KJ3K6GgO8aQJICew0-yHO58M77WApLWF1QJJpOPd8XLFJsViSgb80CHbfEq%7EGJcXUHsCJWFxZo1W5SvHSpnER0cfJhdCjw5fEPOmcznrvEWUUIGSIj7SPWilMrmUVSZyA%7EkDq2wr0Phdhp3%7ELId3eD4Pbxm%7E1SiW5L2hVWtinDACmt1gOUCdtzoadiVwJR6Wmndc3FPoMAIbKdBB2bJDdDNYqkPmy6z5RgNcYZFuZZen4QODjWGUc7H27ijiAeStKYd2r-Dib%7EjE0tqCQyVxK9C4Yf4mVhiQ9ktbrQb95ug__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIUCZBIA4LVPAVW3Q\" alt=\" Overview of the applied preprocessing steps and approaches. Preprocessing workflows from left to right: Limitation of the coverage and smoothing of methylation levels are part of BiSeq and were also applied before using Global Test and Limma/ z -test. Filtering out CpG sites in samples with low coverage and regions with few CpG sites are part of COHCAP. Filtering out CpG sites in all samples that were lowly covered in at least one sample, limitation of the coverage and summarization of the read counts were applied before using Poisson, quasi-Poisson and negative binomial regression. Removing CpG sites in all samples that were not covered in all samples is part of methylKit. There were no preprocessing or filtering steps in the RADMeth/ z -test pipeline. For the simulated data, we applied the preprocessing steps exactly as shown here. For the CLL data, which had more samples, we slightly adjusted the filter for Poisson, quasi-Poisson and negative binomial regression: We filtered out CpG sites in all samples that had coverage &lt;3 in &gt;25% of the samples in either group (CLL or healthy). A colour version of this figure is available online at BIB online: http://bib.oxfordjournals.org . \"><br><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spa