     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/AKElOhbRcX50yR7SLpsje6Yo1vX2AoBtmTrOuD16nJxo9EzluxgaEjbrVHO_nv8Vvw-SSc_p5A6sOhbwV2aDbMN9VMuaHYfPU61P5QCoMFCiDcnRQXXe8eaMvUGMBpQUUdI9FF_ARXtfo7Jr2vN3q9ygORImoLAOCsHRGdAaCPfDDeJOgwtymUYkcgRJgn8osKzHCy7JhozFs7A5XtcqooVYsJuT4XjZcuqOqfGYVibeHnGGv0b84y1LjIeUsRP3d_DZGw-vHzUc6RdaTIfenfI6XksrG2mru699XIIoVDU-6DGJMhdIjWub6J6j_G69iSScDnroQWsZswY5wUTt7muO0Eeq9JNaLVE74vyrmiwMlJS7EVfM7Tt7-DtgKi1mFou-2587Tvcknvi0EYahlglT9twssrTNn5DWBs3-daCpynoxdsb-X_i2yyzu2-V6hgX9zBbFQqJOE7B0C9jdATas5QX97rZWIOciWPpTkhxwTOUOm-4O4lVnKYP0AzVhNiSoWkPwHpInPKjlNiZ5OYp8o_7nU1Av6Kt1twjDlILrCeae5AqpMcefI53Eca7nflO8uKGkxID9gki-ER9oWGe9Gg5wo-50D_qoS__eeXDn6x87ye8mMt29zrdZJu4jIw2D4Qk-yqanDKyjDJEaMk8rxZ1Avlgl8O_lsJbifE-op_sMWt6DOokKpjmlYV36zNmeJerR2UQNSKGlMXtdOFcD_78S0Skv-TE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://oup.silverchair-cdn.com/oup/backfile/Content_public/Journal/bib/17/5/10.1093_bib_bbv095/2/m_bbv095f2p.png?Expires=1490972949&amp;Signature=DxriMJ1BF%7E9YrSi%7E2zqmZaMKYyKlFtQH3m3yaqekyG-KJ3K6GgO8aQJICew0-yHO58M77WApLWF1QJJpOPd8XLFJsViSgb80CHbfEq%7EGJcXUHsCJWFxZo1W5SvHSpnER0cfJhdCjw5fEPOmcznrvEWUUIGSIj7SPWilMrmUVSZyA%7EkDq2wr0Phdhp3%7ELId3eD4Pbxm%7E1SiW5L2hVWtinDACmt1gOUCdtzoadiVwJR6Wmndc3FPoMAIbKdBB2bJDdDNYqkPmy6z5RgNcYZFuZZen4QODjWGUc7H27ijiAeStKYd2r-Dib%7EjE0tqCQyVxK9C4Yf4mVhiQ9ktbrQb95ug__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIUCZBIA4LVPAVW3Q\" alt=\" Overview of the applied preprocessing steps and approaches. Preprocessing workflows from left to right: Limitation of the coverage and smoothing of methylation levels are part of BiSeq and were also applied before using Global Test and Limma/ z -test. Filtering out CpG sites in samples with low coverage and regions with few CpG sites are part of COHCAP. Filtering out CpG sites in all samples that were lowly covered in at least one sample, limitation of the coverage and summarization of the read counts were applied before using Poisson, quasi-Poisson and negative binomial regression. Removing CpG sites in all samples that were not covered in all samples is part of methylKit. There were no preprocessing or filtering steps in the RADMeth/ z -test pipeline. For the simulated data, we applied the preprocessing steps exactly as shown here. For the CLL data, which had more samples, we slightly adjusted the filter for Poisson, quasi-Poisson and negative binomial regression: We filtered out CpG sites in all samples that had coverage &lt;3 in &gt;25% of the samples in either group (CLL or healthy). A colour version of this figure is available online at BIB online: http://bib.oxfordjournals.org . \"><br><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666984558105px\">Cheers,</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt\">Chris</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;vertical-align:middle\">----------------------------------------------</div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;vertical-align:middle\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(232,119,34)\">Christopher E. Mason, Ph.D.</span></b></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\">Associate Professor</div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Department of Physiology and Biophysics </span></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;vertical-align:middle\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(179,27,27)\">Weill Cornell Medicine</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(179,27,27)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(115,112,112)\">WorldQuant Foundation Research Scholar</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:13px;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\" color=\"#737070\">Affiliate Fellow, ISP, Yale Law School</font></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;line-height:11.4pt;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(115,112,112)\">(Dry Lab) 1305 York Ave., 13th floor, Y13-04</span></div><div